# Mirror ado pushes to gh-itp

When you push branches to the `ado` remote, push those same branches to `gh-itp` in the same turn.

- `ado`: `https://dev.azure.com/FrontLineCare/Tools/_git/baxter-plugins`
- `gh-itp`: `https://github.com/Hillrom-Enterprise/novum-cursor-plugins.git`

Push only the branch refs that were just sent to `ado`. Leave remote-tracking refs (`refs/remotes/*`) local.

```bash
git push ado <branch>
git push gh-itp <branch>
```

Do not use `git push --mirror`. That publishes remote-tracking refs and deletes branches on `gh-itp` that are not present locally.

If `gh-itp` rejects the update because it is not a fast-forward, stop and report the divergence. Do not force-push unless the user explicitly says to overwrite `gh-itp` history.
